), launched by Font Awesome, aimed at making it easier for anyone to build, publish, and maintain websites. The campaign is live and backers are encouraged to support it directly on Kickstarter.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/454367a43b5675213829c16576da8a01?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29T14:42:05.892Z"},{"id":"UWOBu8bo3","title":"Collaborative Editing as Progressive Enhancement\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/collaborative-editing/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/collaborative-editing-as-progressive-enhancement-zachleat-com-uwobu8bo3","summary":"A case is made for building a new web site builder that layers on top of existing projects as a progressive enhancement, framing infrastructure itself as progressive enhancement. The post is tied to the upcoming Build awesome (11ty) kickstarter campaign launching April 28, 2026.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/406d96abe91aae3bd0309bb0b44b49a1?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-22T19:11:50.627Z"},{"id":"lTdm8ZGWw","title":"AMA about Build Awesome, an Open Town Hall at the 11ty Meetup\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/ama-build-awesome-town-hall/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ama-about-build-awesome-an-open-town-hall-at-the-11ty-meetup-zachleat-com-ltdm8zgww","summary":"Zach Leatherman hosts a 44-minute open town hall AMA at the 11ty Meetup, fielding community questions about the Eleventy static site generator's rebrand to 'Build Awesome'. The session is available to watch on YouTube.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/16a65a3ad357e613414a7291aadda50b?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-17T01:16:32.608Z"},{"id":"9N3BO4Sv1","title":"State of the Browser (2026) It\u2019s 10PM: Do You Know Where Your JavaScript Is?\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/its-10pm/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/state-of-the-browser-2026-it-s-10pm-do-you-know-where-your-javascript-is-zachleat-com-9n3bo4sv1","summary":"A conference talk from State of the Browser 2026 exploring best practices around JavaScript usage on the web. The talk examines how to find the right JavaScript footprint for a website \u2014 addressing both over-reliance on JS and whether zero-JavaScript is a realistic goal. Supporting links cover web history (HTML 1992, CSS1), progressive enhancement, CDN caching pitfalls, the polyfill supply chain attack, Subresource Integrity, responsive design, CSS-in-JS libraries, and server-side rendering definitions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/58de412310787163b0819982075f6911?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-17T01:16:32.607Z"},{"id":"PZ6zrdVqq","title":"Eleventy, 2025 in Review\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/eleventy-2025-review/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/eleventy-2025-in-review-zachleat-com-pz6zrdvqq","summary":"Eleventy had a strong 2025 with 177 releases (73% increase), 804 closed issues (15% increase), and 51% growth in npm downloads. The project reduced its dependency count by 28% and package weight by 22%, while continuing to grow its user base.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6ff9e01fe43549d2d987bd581b15b408?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-12T22:03:48.166Z"},{"id":"G7eqoN0ig","title":"State of the Browser 2026\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/state-of-the-browser/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/state-of-the-browser-2026-zachleat-com-g7eqon0ig","summary":"State of the Browser 2026 is a web development conference taking place in the United Kingdom. The event features talks about browser technologies and web standards, with tickets currently available for purchase.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f6a9b972b93086bafbc8428115cf8f47?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-12T22:03:48.127Z"},{"id":"5CsI2gG7J","title":"No more tokens! Locking down npm Publish Workflows\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/npm-security/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/no-more-tokens-locking-down-npm-publish-workflows-zachleat-com-5csi2gg7j","summary":"Comprehensive guide to securing npm package publishing workflows in response to recent supply chain attacks. Covers eliminating access tokens in favor of OIDC Trusted Publishers, implementing 2FA requirements, using password managers, pinning GitHub Actions dependencies, checking in lock files, and restricting publishing access. Includes detailed security checklist with specific configuration steps for GitHub and npm, plus additional recommendations like immutable releases and package manager cooldowns.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/20e9dc1ed5e61c307558cc05ef67371e?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-04T04:13:43.984Z"},{"id":"dXg43islI","title":"Creating AI-style text animations with web components","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/hallucinate/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-hallucinate-using-web-components-zachleat-com-dxg43isli","summary":"A satirical tutorial demonstrating how to create an AI-like text animation effect using the <squirm-inal> Web Component. The component progressively animates pre-written content to mimic chatbot typing patterns, offering a humorous alternative to actual LLM-generated text. Implementation requires wrapping HTML content in the custom element with configurable speed and autoplay attributes, using CDN delivery with subresource integrity for security.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/09365b7250eb37b691f29751ddfe2c91?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-25T14:06:34.181Z"},{"id":"418Dn5M8g","title":"How we use GitHub Issues (on 11ty) and how that\u2019s Changing\u2014zachleat.com","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/11ty-github-issues/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-we-use-github-issues-on-11ty-and-how-that-s-changing-zachleat-com-418dn5m8g","summary":"Explores the workflow and practices for managing GitHub Issues in the Eleventy (11ty) static site generator project, discussing current approaches and upcoming changes to issue tracking and project management processes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f9f0dd0ce05f9d48290ba99436dba75f?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-03T23:32:28.157Z"},{"id":"xChOTiLas","title":"Adding copy buttons to code blocks with Web Awesome and Eleventy","url":"https://www.zachleat.com/web/copy-paste/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/copy-and-paste-in-this-economy-zachleat-com-xchotilas","summary":"Implementation guide for adding copy-to-clipboard functionality to code blocks using Web Awesome's custom element component. Covers progressive enhancement approach with JavaScript-only behavior, performance optimization through build-time bundling with esbuild, and lazy loading with is-land. Includes practical configuration examples for integrating the copy button component into Eleventy documentation sites, with options for both CDN delivery and custom bundling.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9c4f7eed119ee5aa8b0f9ec929a14def?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-28T21:36:58.658Z"}],"similar_handles":["disney","ember","k8s","redwoodjs","python"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","ryolu_","kloss_xyz","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"disney","handle":"disney","name":"The Art of Possible","is_squad":false,"x":-7.7459,"y":-3.5679,"cluster_id"